k></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMADA MASAHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAIKIN INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIWARI, KAZUO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA, TATSURO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, MASAHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIWARI KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA TATSURO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMADA MASAHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIWARI, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA, TATSURO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, MASAHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A PTFE laminate which contains a PTFE sheet retaining a high specific gravity and has sufficient adhesion strength; and a PTFE-based backing sheet reduced in permeability to liquid chemicals. The laminate is produced by fusion-bonding a PTFE sheet to a film or sheet of a fusible resin such as PFA, with a layer of fine PTFE particles interposed therebetween or without the layer, and then subjecting the laminate to a treatment in which it is prevented from rapidly cooling. Thus, the average specific gravity of the PTFE sheet is kept at 2.175 or higher.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un laminé en PTFE qui comprend une feuille en PTFE ayant un poids spécifique élevé et une force d'adhérence suffisante, ainsi qu'une feuille de fond à base de PTFE à perméabilité réduite aux substances chimiques liquides. On produit ce laminé en assemblant par fusion une feuille en PTFE et un film ou une feuille d'une résine fusible telle que PFA avec une couche de petites particules PTFE, entreposées entre ces feuilles ou films ou placées hors de cette couche, et en soumettant le laminé à un traitement qui l'empêche de refroidir rapidement. Cela permet de garder le poids spécifique de la feuille en PTFE à la hauteur ou au-dessus de 2,175.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>